    "done_when": "Produce and validate the host flight file for §3 of docs/plans/lane-and-model-routing.html, exactly as that section states. The plan and its locked decisions (dialect-names, imply-when-unique, when-undeclared) are the authority. §1 and §2 are on main. Do not edit any repository: the coordinator applies your validated file to the dotfiles repository afterwards.\n\n1. Copy the live host flight /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/dotfiles/reckon/flight.yaml into your report directory as flight.before.yaml. Write flight.yaml beside it, in which one lanes.claude block replaces backends.claude, backends.claude-opus and backends.claude-haiku. The one real difference, opus's 40-minute time budget against the lane's 25, becomes a per-model time_budget override on opus. Keep every comment and every other block unchanged, so the diff against flight.before.yaml is only the claude collapse.\n2. Validate with the reckon main checkout's interpreter (/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/reckon), pointing RECKON_FLIGHT_CONFIG at the file under test. Never touch the live host flight.\n   - For every project in ~/.config/reckon/mounts.json, the resolved flight with flight.yaml is identical to the one with flight.before.yaml. Keep each pair and the diff.\n   - reckon flight reports three entries under lane claude, two of them derived.\n   - The derived claude-opus entry resolves to the same model, effort, time budget and launch argv that the retired block produced.\n3. Negative control: a copy of flight.yaml without opus's time_budget override resolves claude-opus to 25 minutes and fails the equivalence check.\n\nDeliver flight.before.yaml, flight.yaml, flight.diff, the per-project comparison logs (each ending in an EXIT line) and a report.md in the report directory.",
